All set — I followed DE_Guide_v10_1.md and completed the extraction into DE_Kim2023_by_codex_20251123002128.json.

Highlights
- Study: Kim2023; Nature Mental Health (2024); DOI 10.1038/s44220-024-00297-z
- Reference cohort: N=54,102 controls across 132 sites; age 54.44±20.25 (derived); sex 53%F/47%M
- Imaging: T1-weighted MRI; lobular volumes (ACAPULCO) and voxel-wise GM maps (SUIT; Jacobian-modulated)
- Preprocessing: FreeSurfer 5.3; FSL (reorient + FLIRT v6.0); ACAPULCO v0.2.1 (ENIGMA v3.1; N4 + ANTs ICBM 2009c); SUIT v3.4; intensity normalization to [0,1]
- Model: New; PCNtoolkit v0.24 (Python 3.8); Bayesian linear regression with likelihood warping (sinarcsinsh); site fixed effect
- Validation: Independent same-domain (site/sex/age stratified train/test); no non‑independent or different-domain validation
- QC: ENIGMA cerebellum QC with Singularity; ACAPULCO QC; exclude outliers ≥2 regions and sites <5 participants; ~5% manual inspection
- Clinical: ASD (900); BD (277); SZ (312); AD (146); MCI (122); datasets ABIDE (ASD), TOP (SZ/BD), ADNI/AIBL/DEMGEN (AD/MCI)
- Deviations: z-scores; extreme |z|>1.96; ASD/MCI show more positive/negative extremes; SZ/AD predominantly negative; deviations associate with IQ

If you want, I can also produce a short changelog or run a quick diff to show exactly what fields were populated.
